<cem:title lang="" subtitle="">Welcome Home Party</cem:title>
<cem:description lang="">This virtual learning object "Welcome Home Party" that makes part of the lesson No: 1, John Comes Home for a Visit, which in turn belongs to the Elementary (A2.2) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, is intended to work on: make and respond to request; talk or report about things, actions, events, or people. The grammar of this LO refers to: modals for requests: can, could; simple past tense in affirmative sentences to talk about past events, e.g. I loved Mexico. Also, the vocabulary considers: food, e.g.taco, pork, shrimp.</cem:description>
<cem:keyword lang="">
<cem:li>Describing plans</cem:li>
<cem:li>Organizing events</cem:li>
<cem:li>Making simple requests</cem:li>
<cem:li>Responding to requests</cem:li>
<cem:li>Can</cem:li>
<cem:li>Could</cem:li>
<cem:li>Simple past tense</cem:li>
<cem:li>Talking about food</cem:li>
</cem:keyword>
