<cem:description>
<cem:recommendedUse lang="en">This digital resource can be used as an activity that allows the learner to reflect on the use of grammar of English language in different communicative contexts. The instructor can work further on activities and tasks that help learners to improve their procedural knowledge.</cem:recommendedUse>
<cem:triggerQuestion lang="en">What did you do yesterday?; What did you do last week?; What did you do last month?</cem:triggerQuestion>
<cem:pedagogicalAspect lang="en">This learning object "Welcome Home Party" that is part of the lesson No: 1, John Comes Home for a Visit, which in turn belongs to the Elementary (A2.2) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, allows the learner to develop the following topics: modals for requests: can, could; simple past tense in affirmative sentences to talk about past events, e.g. I loved Mexico. It is presented within the context of make and respond to request; talk or report about things, actions, events, or people. The student will be exposed to vocabulary related to: food, e.g.taco, pork, shrimp. Learners will develop their language skills by using an online content as well as the guidance of a SENA instructor.</cem:pedagogicalAspect>
<cem:learningGoal lang="en">The purpose of this learning object is to identify and describe plans for the organization of events.</cem:learningGoal>
</cem:description>
</cem:educational>
